From 0a58b5965ae3f837050279d938fa176533788dda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Agathe Porte <agathe.porte@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:03:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tqtfp-populate-readwrite: use libexec instead of usrbin

meson currently installs `/usr/bin/populate-readwrite.sh`, which is not
great in a distro context:

 * The name is too generic as nothing ties it to the tqftpserv package;
 * The .sh extension should not appear in /usr/bin/

The second point is raised via the script-with-language-extension
lintian tag.

Move the script to a new `/usr/libexec/tqftpserv/` directory to fix the
two listed issues.

Closes: #57

Signed-off-by: Agathe Porte <agathe.porte@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 meson.build                             | 2 +-
 tqftpserv-populate-readwrite.service.in | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 4979cf0..33ff571 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ executable('tqftpserv',
 configure_file(
   input : 'populate-readwrite.sh',
   output : 'populate-readwrite.sh',
-  install_dir : prefix / 'bin',
+  install_dir : prefix / 'libexec' / 'tqftpserv',
   copy : true)
 
 if systemd_system_unit_dir != ''
diff --git a/tqftpserv-populate-readwrite.service.in b/tqftpserv-populate-readwrite.service.in
index 5da4363..0f6416f 100644
--- a/tqftpserv-populate-readwrite.service.in
+++ b/tqftpserv-populate-readwrite.service.in
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ Before=tqftpserv.service
 
 [Service]
 Type=oneshot
-ExecStart=@prefix@/bin/populate-readwrite.sh
+ExecStart=@prefix@/libexec/tqftpserv/populate-readwrite.sh
 
 [Install]
 WantedBy=multi-user.target
-- 
